---
import { ArrowRight, BookOpen, Building2, FileText, Flag, LockKeyhole, MessageCircle, PencilLine, ShieldCheck } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ProductContextBar from '../../components/ProductContextBar.astro';

const trail = [
	{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
	{ name: 'Design', path: '/design/commons-preview' },
	{ name: 'Thread preview', path: '/design/thread-preview' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Commons thread preview"
	description="Internal Birch Commons thread specimen showing the future read-only conversation, research bridge, contribution lanes, and moderation boundary."
	noindex
	pageType="editorial"
>
	<section class="band band-tight band-first band-paper thread-preview-hero">
		<div class="shell">
			<Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />
			<ProductContextBar active="commons" />
			<div class="thread-preview-state"><span class="status status-plain">Internal product specimen</span><span class="mono">Read-only · no live activity</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band band-tight band-paper thread-preview-band" aria-labelledby="thread-title">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="thread-preview-shell">
				<aside class="thread-room-rail" aria-label="Commons room navigation">
					<div class="thread-room-brand">
						<span class="eyebrow">Birch Commons</span>
						<strong>Real people.<br />Clearer insurance.</strong>
					</div>
					<nav class="thread-room-nav" aria-label="Conversation rooms">
						<a class="is-active" href="/design/commons-preview#threads"><MessageCircle size={16} aria-hidden="true" /><span>All conversations</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
						<a href="/insurance"><BookOpen size={16} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Homeowners</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
						<a href="/insurance"><ShieldCheck size={16} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Auto</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
						<a href="/insurance"><Building2 size={16} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Business insurance</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
						<a href="/professionals"><PencilLine size={16} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Professional notes</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
					</nav>
					<div class="thread-room-note"><span class="meta">No popularity ranking</span><p>Rooms are organized by context and moderation state, not by a reputation score.</p></div>
					<div class="thread-room-footer"><span>A more informed</span><strong>insurance world.</strong></div>
				</aside>

				<main class="thread-reading-column">
					<nav class="thread-local-crumbs" aria-label="Thread location"><a href="/design/commons-preview">Commons preview</a><ArrowRight size={12} aria-hidden="true" /><a href="/insurance">Homeowners</a><ArrowRight size={12} aria-hidden="true" /><span aria-current="page">Experience</span></nav>
					<span class="thread-type-chip">Experience</span>
					<h1 id="thread-title">The renewal notice arrived before I understood what changed</h1>
					<div class="thread-author-row">
						<div class="thread-avatar" aria-hidden="true">R</div>
						<div><strong>Reader · identity protected in specimen</strong><span>Specimen state · future thread</span></div>
						<span class="thread-author-meta mono">Illustrative only</span>
					</div>
					<div class="thread-body">
						<p>I received a homeowners renewal notice and the changes were not clear to me. The coverage limits looked similar, but the documents used different terms and the amount due changed.</p>
						<p>I wanted to understand what to compare in the renewal packet before asking a professional for help. This is a question about reading the documents, not a conclusion about why a particular change happened.</p>
					</div>

					<div class="thread-research-bridge" aria-label="Research context">
						<span class="thread-research-label">Additional<br />context</span>
						<a href="/ask"><BookOpen size={18} aria-hidden="true" /><span><strong>Research this question</strong><small>Guides and answers from Birch Research</small></span><ArrowRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
						<a href="/sources"><FileText size={18} aria-hidden="true" /><span><strong>Open source ledger</strong><small>See how a topic is documented</small></span><ArrowRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
					</div>

					<div class="thread-replies" aria-labelledby="replies-title">
						<div class="thread-section-label"><span class="eyebrow" id="replies-title">Contextual replies</span><span class="mono">Specimen states</span></div>
						<article class="thread-reply thread-reply-professional">
							<div class="thread-reply-icon"><ShieldCheck size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></div>
							<div><div class="thread-reply-head"><span class="thread-reply-type">Professional note</span><span class="mono">Role disclosed · specimen</span></div><p>Renewal documents can change in more places than the headline limit. A careful comparison would look at deductibles, sub-limits, exclusions, endorsements, valuation language, and any change in the form edition.</p></div>
						</article>
						<article class="thread-reply thread-reply-company">
							<div class="thread-reply-icon"><Building2 size={17} aria-hidden="true" /></div>
							<div><div class="thread-reply-head"><span class="thread-reply-type">Company response</span><span class="mono">Organization verification required · specimen</span></div><p>An attributed response can explain a process or point to an official document. It cannot remove the original account or change Birch’s sourced research.</p></div>
						</article>
					</div>

					<div class="thread-join-gate" aria-labelledby="join-title">
						<div class="thread-join-icon"><LockKeyhole size={18} aria-hidden="true" /></div>
						<div><h2 id="join-title">Sign in to join the conversation.</h2><p>Accounts and moderation are not enabled in this preview.</p></div>
						<button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Sign in <ArrowRight size={15} aria-hidden="true" /></button>
					</div>
				</main>

				<aside class="thread-context-rail" aria-label="Thread context and tools">
					<div class="thread-context-card">
						<div class="thread-context-icon"><BookOpen size={18} aria-hidden="true" /></div>
						<span class="eyebrow">Research stays primary</span>
						<h2>Conversation is context, not marketing.</h2>
						<p>Explore the public research before deciding what a thread adds or leaves unanswered.</p>
						<a class="text-link" href="/explore">Explore research <ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
					</div>
					<div class="thread-context-card">
						<div class="thread-context-icon"><ShieldCheck size={18} aria-hidden="true" /></div>
						<span class="eyebrow">This thread is not a verdict</span>
						<p>Commons is for experiences and perspectives. It is not personalized advice and it does not replace professional counsel or policy documents.</p>
						<a class="text-link" href="/methodology">Read the boundary <ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
					</div>
					<div class="thread-tools">
						<span class="eyebrow">Thread tools</span>
						<button type="button" disabled><Flag size={15} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Report</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></button>
						<button type="button" disabled><PencilLine size={15} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Request correction</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></button>
						<button type="button" disabled><LockKeyhole size={15} aria-hidden="true" /><span>Withdraw contribution</span><ArrowRight size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></button>
						<p class="mono">Future controls · unavailable in specimen</p>
					</div>
					<div class="thread-specimen-stamp"><span class="status status-plain">Specimen / future</span><span class="mono">Not live · UI concept only</span></div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.thread-preview-hero { padding-bottom: var(--s-4); }
	.thread-preview-hero .crumbs { margin-bottom: var(--s-4); }
	.thread-preview-state { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-3); }
	.thread-preview-band { padding-top: var(--s-4); }
	.thread-preview-shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 190px minmax(0, 1fr) 260px; gap: 1px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--r-4); background: var(--line-strong); box-shadow: var(--elev-2); }
	.thread-room-rail, .thread-reading-column, .thread-context-rail { min-width: 0; background: var(--paper); }
	.thread-room-rail { display: flex; min-height: 900px; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--s-5); }
	.thread-room-brand { padding-bottom: var(--s-5); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.thread-room-brand .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--s-2); }
	.thread-room-brand strong { color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 400; line-height: var(--leading-snug); }
	.thread-room-nav { display: grid; gap: 4px; margin-top: var(--s-5); }
	.thread-room-nav a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 18px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: var(--s-2); align-items: center; padding: 9px 7px; border-radius: var(--r-2); color: var(--body); font-size: var(--text-sm); text-decoration: none; transition: background var(--dur-1) var(--ease), color var(--dur-1) var(--ease), padding-left var(--dur-2) var(--ease-soft); }
	.thread-room-nav a:hover, .thread-room-nav a:focus-visible, .thread-room-nav a.is-active { background: var(--brand-blue-wash); color: var(--brand-blue-deep); }
	.thread-room-nav a:hover, .thread-room-nav a:focus-visible { padding-left: 10px; }
	.thread-room-note { margin-top: auto; padding-top: var(--s-4); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.thread-room-note p { margin: var(--s-2) 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-xs); line-height: var(--leading-snug); }
	.thread-room-footer { padding-top: var(--s-5); margin-top: var(--s-5); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-lg); font-style: italic; line-height: var(--leading-snug); }
	.thread-room-footer span, .thread-room-footer strong { display: block; }
	.thread-room-footer strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 400; }
	.thread-reading-column { padding: clamp(var(--s-5), 4vw, var(--s-8)); }
	.thread-local-crumbs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: var(--s-5); color: var(--muted); font: var(--text-2xs)/1.3 var(--font-mono); }
	.thread-local-crumbs a { color: var(--brand-blue-text); text-decoration: none; }
	.thread-local-crumbs a:hover, .thread-local-crumbs a:focus-visible { text-decoration: underline; }
	.thread-type-chip, .thread-reply-type { color: var(--brand-blue-text); font: var(--text-2xs)/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.thread-type-chip { display: inline-block; padding: 6px 8px; border-radius: var(--r-2); background: var(--brand-blue-wash); }
	.thread-reading-column h1 { max-width: 18ch; margin: var(--s-4) 0 var(--s-5); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem); letter-spacing: -.03em; }
	.thread-author-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-3); padding-bottom: var(--s-5); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.thread-avatar { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 40px; height: 40px; flex: 0 0 auto; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--blue-wash); color: var(--brand-blue-text); font: var(--text-sm)/1 var(--font-mono); }
	.thread-author-row strong, .thread-author-row span { display: block; }
	.thread-author-row strong { color: var(--ink); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
	.thread-author-row span { margin-top: 3px; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
	.thread-author-row .thread-author-meta { margin: 0 0 0 auto; color: var(--faint); }
	.thread-body { max-width: 68ch; padding-top: var(--s-5); }
	.thread-body p { margin: 0; color: var(--body); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-lg); line-height: 1.55; }
	.thread-body p + p { margin-top: var(--s-4); }
	.thread-research-bridge { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 82px minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1px; margin-top: var(--s-6); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-3); background: var(--line); }
	.thread-research-label { display: grid; place-items: center; padding: var(--s-3); background: var(--blue-wash); color: var(--brand-blue-text); font: var(--text-2xs)/1.4 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-align: center; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.thread-research-bridge a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 20px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: var(--s-2); align-items: center; padding: var(--s-3); background: var(--paper); color: var(--brand-blue-text); text-decoration: none; transition: background var(--dur-1) var(--ease); }
	.thread-research-bridge a:hover, .thread-research-bridge a:focus-visible { background: var(--brand-blue-wash); }
	.thread-research-bridge strong, .thread-research-bridge small { display: block; }
	.thread-research-bridge strong { font-size: var(--text-sm); }
	.thread-research-bridge small { margin-top: 3px; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-2xs); line-height: var(--leading-snug); }
	.thread-replies { margin-top: var(--s-8); }
	.thread-section-label { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--s-3); padding-bottom: var(--s-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
	.thread-section-label .eyebrow { margin: 0; }
	.thread-reply { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 36px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s-3); padding: var(--s-5) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.thread-reply-icon, .thread-context-icon, .thread-join-icon { display: grid; place-items: center; }
	.thread-reply-icon { width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold-wash); color: var(--gold-text); }
	.thread-reply-company .thread-reply-icon { background: var(--brand-blue); color: #fff; }
	.thread-reply-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--s-3); }
	.thread-reply p { max-width: 68ch; margin: var(--s-2) 0 0; color: var(--body); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-base); line-height: var(--leading-normal); }
	.thread-join-gate { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 38px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: var(--s-3); align-items: center; padding: var(--s-4); margin-top: var(--s-6); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-3); background: var(--blue-wash); }
	.thread-join-icon { width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--paper); color: var(--brand-blue-text); }
	.thread-join-gate h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 400; }
	.thread-join-gate p { margin: 3px 0 0; color: var(--brand-blue-text); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
	.thread-context-rail { display: grid; align-content: start; gap: 1px; background: var(--line); }
	.thread-context-card, .thread-tools, .thread-specimen-stamp { padding: var(--s-5); background: var(--paper); }
	.thread-context-icon { width: 36px; height: 36px; margin-bottom: var(--s-4); border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold-wash); color: var(--gold-text); }
	.thread-context-card h2 { margin: var(--s-2) 0 var(--s-3); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 400; line-height: var(--leading-snug); }
	.thread-context-card p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: var(--leading-normal); }
	.thread-context-card .text-link { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; margin-top: var(--s-4); color: var(--brand-blue-text); font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
	.thread-tools { display: grid; gap: var(--s-2); }
	.thread-tools .eyebrow { margin-bottom: var(--s-1); }
	.thread-tools button { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 18px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: var(--s-2); align-items: center; width: 100%; min-height: var(--tap); padding: 8px var(--s-3); border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--r-2); background: var(--paper); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); text-align: left; }
	.thread-tools button:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: .72; }
	.thread-tools .mono { margin: var(--s-2) 0 0; color: var(--faint); font-size: var(--text-2xs); }
	.thread-specimen-stamp { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--s-2); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
	@media (max-width: 1060px) {
		.thread-preview-shell { grid-template-columns: 170px minmax(0, 1fr) 230px; }
		.thread-reading-column { padding: var(--s-5); }
		.thread-room-rail { padding-inline: var(--s-4); }
	}
	@media (max-width: 820px) {
		.thread-preview-shell { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
		.thread-room-rail { min-height: 0; }
		.thread-room-note, .thread-room-footer { display: none; }
		.thread-room-nav { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
		.thread-context-rail { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
		.thread-tools, .thread-specimen-stamp { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
	}
	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.thread-room-nav, .thread-context-rail { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
		.thread-room-nav a { padding-block: 11px; }
		.thread-reading-column { padding: var(--s-4); }
		.thread-reading-column h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 10vw, 3rem); }
		.thread-author-row .thread-author-meta { width: 100%; margin-left: 52px; }
		.thread-research-bridge { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
		.thread-research-label { place-items: start; text-align: left; }
		.thread-join-gate { grid-template-columns: 36px minmax(0, 1fr); }
		.thread-join-gate .btn { grid-column: 1 / -1; width: 100%; }
	}
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.thread-room-nav a, .thread-research-bridge a { transition: none; }
	}
</style>
